Tweaks from Scubrah's Patch, Realism Plus and FC2JackalFix, each one a setting you switch in game instead of a patched [font=Courier New]Dunia.dll[/font] you have to install. Nothing on disk is overwritten, nothing is left behind when you remove it, and every setting leaves the game exactly as it shipped until you change it.

Using one of those mods for its data? Keep it. This plugin supplies only the engine side of their tweaks, so you no longer need their patched [font=Courier New]Dunia.dll[/font].

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
In [b]Options → Mod Configuration Menu → LegacyPlugin[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]Briefings keep control[/b] - a briefing no longer stands you up and takes control away.[/*]
[*][b]Keep weapon on rescue[/b] - a buddy rescue no longer swaps out your secondary weapon.[/*]
[*][b]No forced buddy rescues[/b] - the factions stop assigning buddy rescue missions, so a bugged one can't block the story. Takes effect from the next launch; start a new game after changing it.[/*]
[*][b]No reputation drop[/b] - finishing A1SM03 or A2SM08 no longer lowers your reputation.[/*]
[*][b]Hide diamond message[/b] - picking up diamonds no longer shows the game's own message, for mods that show their own.[/*]
[*][b]No blinking pickups[/b] - weapons, ammo, health, diamond cases and other usable things stop flashing, and so do map and compass markers.[/*]
[*][b]No save icons on map[/b] - save points lose their icon on the map and the GPS, from the next reload.[/*]
[*][b]Limited saving[/b] - Save Game leaves the pause menu and F5/F9 stop working. Save points and autosaves still save.[/*]
[*][b]Brown filter[/b] - on by default, the game's own colour grade. Off gives a neutral grade without the brown-orange tint.[/*]
[*][b]No hit indicator[/b] - no directional indicators when you take damage.[/*]
[*][b]HUD fade-out[/b] - how long the health, ammo and equipment counters stay up: always hidden, 1 to 60 seconds, or always shown.[/*]
[*][b]Skip tutorial pop-ups[/b] - off, the pop-ups that interrupt play, or those and the floating hints.[/*]
[*][b]Aim toggle[/b] - tap aim to stay in the sights, tap again to lower them.[/*]
[*][b]Sprint toggle[/b] - tap sprint to keep running until you tap again or stop. Keyboard only; the gamepad already has a sprint lock.[/*]
[*][b]Sprint turn[/b] - sprinting no longer slows how fast you turn.[/*]
[*][b]No rim lighting[/b] - removes the glow outlining characters, mostly seen at night.[/*]
[*][b]No sprint and aim blur[/b] - removes the screen blur while sprinting and aiming down the sights.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]How to install (Vortex)[/size][/b]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/about/vortex/]Vortex[/url] and its Far Cry 2 extension.[/*]
[*]Click [b]Mod Manager Download[/b] on this page and enable the mod. Vortex also offers to get [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url], which this mod needs.[/*]
[*]Start the game with the [b]Play[/b] button in Vortex.[/*]
[/list]
Not using Vortex? Install it with JackAll instead, [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url] for JackAll installation. Or by hand: copy [font=Courier New]plugins\LegacyPlugin.dll[/font] into the game's [font=Courier New]bin\plugins[/font] folder and start the game with [font=Courier New]FCSE.exe[/font].

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Needs Far Cry 2 patch 1.03[/b], Steam or GOG, and FCSE 1.4.0 or later.[/*]
[*][b]Don't use it together with a patched [font=Courier New]Dunia.dll[/font] or with FC2JackalFix.[/b] They change the same code.[/*]
[*][b]With Sky Overhaul's Grade on Overhaul[/b], the Brown filter setting has no visible effect: Sky Overhaul's own grade is drawn over it.[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]bin\fcse.log[/font] lists every tweak that was applied.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Credits[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Scubrah's Patch[/b] by scubrah: briefings, buddy rescues, reputation, the diamond message and the neutral colour grade.[/*]
[*][b]Realism Plus[/b] by Boggalog: blinking pickups, save icons and limited saving.[/*]
